.TH GLISSANDO 1 "" "glissando" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glissando \- private on-screen keyboard for Phosh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glissando
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glissando
is an on-screen keyboard for Wayland phones with glide typing, prediction,
auto-correction, emoji and clipboard panels. It works offline. The session
normally starts it through the Phosh-OSK alternative.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take over sm.puri.OSK0 from the running keyboard.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Show immediately, typing with the virtual keyboard until a text field is
focused.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dbus
Do not register on the session bus (for testing).
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-geometry " FILE"
Write key positions as JSON to \fIFILE\fR whenever they change (for testing).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GLISSANDO_DATA_DIR
Extra data directory.
.TP
.B GLISSANDO_CONFIG
Configuration file.
.TP
.B GLISSANDO_DEBUG
Log state changes when not empty. Typed text is never logged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glissando/config.toml
Configuration, written by \fBglissando\-settings\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glissando\-settings (1),
.BR glissando\-voice (1)
